  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi></math> is a point on the line <math><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math><mi>R</mi></math> are two points on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. If the triangle <math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is an equilateral triangle, then its area (in sq. units) is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>15</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "The distance between the given parallel lines <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0090_f2f1b365d25b.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.56667in;height:1.32014in\" /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo></math> Length of the side of the triangle is <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Hence, the area of triangle <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;sq. units"
  }
